evidence. Validation must resolve digests to bounded raw bytes through a sealed resolver contract, re-hash and parse canonical schemas, reject missing, duplicate, extra, relocated, cyclic, oversized, or tampered artifacts, and never trust caller-supplied paths or already-parsed validation flags."},{"id":"separate-capacity-and-cost-effects","statement":"Each measuring cell exposes independently recomputable paired capacity and cost effects. Each effect binds side IDs, numerator and denominator convention, raw values, immutable units, estimate, confidence interval, practical threshold, sample count, and every source digest; capacity is higher-is-better, cost per million correct SLO-eligible operations is lower-is-better, and neither may be inferred from caller-supplied result or claim text."},{"id":"whole-architecture-boundary","statement":"Fixed-resource and fixed-SLO comparisons include every architecture-specific component, provisioned and utilized units, amplification, IOPS, network and inter-zone traffic, minimum footprint, and headroom."},{"id":"immutable-price-projection","statement":"Cost per million correct operations is a separate projection from immutable measured units using a versioned region, date, currency, billing, reservation, and exclusion contract without double counting."},{"id":"harness-fidelity","statement":"Apply the harness-fidelity attack checklist and calibrate synthetic byte and resource counters at live transport, storage, and process seams with immutable raw artifacts."}],"verificationTemplates":[],"frontierIds":["benchmark-whole-topology-resource-accounting-final-main"]}}
